Conducting thorough analysis of existing processes to identify inefficiencies, bottlenecks, and areas for improvement;
Leading initiatives to streamline workflows and eliminate non-value-added activities;
Utilising data analytics and performance metrics to identify trends, assess process performance, and drive data-driven decision-making;
Providing training and guidance to employees at all levels on continuous improvement methodologies;
Implementing and communicating effective change management strategies to ensure safe and smooth adoption of new processes and practices;
Identifying opportunities for the integration of new technologies and automation to improve efficiency and reduce manual intervention;
Identifying and assess potential risks associated with process changes and implement risk mitigation strategies;
Maintaining accurate documentation of processes, changes, and improvements.
Ensuring all activities are conducted at or above Orica’s standards.
What you will bring
Lean Six Sigma Green Belt certified or other continuous improvement methodologies;
Proven experience in leading continuous improvement initiatives in a manufacturing or electronics environment;
Strong analytical, problem-solving, and project management skills;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
1 – 3 years experience in the manufacturing environment;
